cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "llama-roofline: a portable memory-bandwidth roofline for llama.cpp"
message: "If you use this tool in a publication or benchmark report, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Manu Nicholas"
    family-names: "Jacob"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6589-6572"
repository-code: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/llama-roofline"
url: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/llama-roofline"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that measures whether llama.cpp token generation on a given
  machine is limited by memory bandwidth. It measures the machine's sustainable
  memory-read bandwidth with a portable microbenchmark, benchmarks the user's own
  GGUF models with llama-bench across a thread sweep, fits the decode roofline
  tok/s = BW_eff / model_bytes, and reports the resulting bandwidth utilisation
  together with the optimal quantization and thread configuration.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - large language models
  - roofline model
  - memory bandwidth
  - quantization
  - edge inference
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-07"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "llama.cpp"
    authors:
      - name: "The llama.cpp contributors"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp"
    license: MIT
    notes: "The inference engine this tool drives; all throughput numbers come from llama-bench."
